Environment / payment contract
The only accepted Pi PaymentDTO environment is Pi Testnet / testnet (case-normalized), direction=user_to_app.
The PaymentDTO's user_uid, to_address, amount, status, metadata, and transaction verification are verified server-side. Client-submitted values do not authorize settlement.
The expected recipient is the registered Testnet App wallet. Per-project liquidity treasury logic is intentionally not reused.
A stake may only be created after the server-side Pi completion response reports developer completion and the transaction is verified. The RPC is the only path to insert the new investment stake and is restricted to service_role.
Repeated completion/recovery callbacks must return the one original stake for the same payment id.
The public Testnet project registry currently serves only projects with approved or active status. Investment terms must also be active and must match the project, duration, and term ID.
Blocking confirmations before enabling
User provisioning: prove the exact PaymentDTO.user_uid has one matching public.users row with network='testnet'. The RPC fails closed if absent; do not automatically create a user inside settlement.
Reward formula: confirm that Testnet project_staking_terms.reward_rate follows the proposed reward_amount = amount * reward_rate convention. Do not populate or infer missing reward rates. Only active terms are offered by the client.
Testnet App wallet: verify the exact registered Testnet App wallet against the Testnet Pi Developer Portal and deployment configuration; missing wallet configuration must keep the gateway disabled.
Pi Platform contract: verify the returned PaymentDTO/status fields with an isolated Testnet payment. The official Platform API describes U2A as frontend creation followed by server-side approval and completion, and recommends relying on the server completion response rather than client claims.
Payment recovery: confirm handling of cancelled, pending, approved, completed-but-not-verified, and incomplete payment scenarios.
Status change during payment: if a project's eligibility changes after server approval, support/recovery policy must be explicitly tested. Current draft fails closed if the project no longer has an eligible status when the request is re-evaluated; do not silently bypass this rule.
Known limits / non-goals
This package has not been tested against Pi Testnet or PostgreSQL. Syntax checks only prove the JavaScript parses.
The SQL is a draft, not a deploy-ready migration. Use disposable database testing and review first.
Only projects with existing valid active Testnet terms can be tested. Read-only inspection found terms for RAHEEM-25 at 30, 60, and 90 days; this is a time-of-audit observation, not a guarantee it remains unchanged.
This does not provide Mainnet External investment support and does not modify Mainnet Core/Internal gateways.
This does not enable Pi payments, project payouts, treasury funding, or app service payments.
This does not create a Mainnet financial record or asset. Testnet Pi has no Mainnet investment value.
Do not alter existing Dock Navigation or unrelated authentication, withdrawal, dApp Service, liquidity, or payout logic.
